# Host ops: prefer eip over Make

**Preferred host tool:** `eip` / `eip.exe` (admintool). Docs: `docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md` § Dual path.

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Bring up / recover | **`eip up`** (live) / **`eip dev`** (bake) |
| Day-2 YAML / secrets | **`eip sync`** / **`eip secrets`** |
| Local image roll | **`eip rebuild`** |
| Host tool binary | **`eip update-binary`** |
| Data plane ensure | Built into Ready on up/dev; or **`eip ensure-s3`** / **`eip ensure-mongo`** |

## Make leftovers (not eip features)

Do **not** add eip mirrors of these. Prefer the eip column above.

| Legacy Make | Prefer |
|-------------|--------|
| `make release` / `dev-release` / `advertise` | **`eip up`** / **`eip dev`** / **`eip rebuild`** |
| `make update-data SERVICE=` | **`eip up`** / **`eip rebuild`** (pins in stack YAML) |
| `scripts/swarm/stack-deploy.sh` | **`eip up`** / **`eip dev`** (Go calls `docker stack deploy` CLI; no SDK stack-deploy API yet) |
| `make update-files` | Public chicken-egg only (until eip installer exists) |

## Remaining Make verbs (still scripted)

Public/dev helpers that still shell to `scripts/` when someone uses Make: `up`, `dev`, `status`, `logs`, `cli`, `swarm-sync`, `swarm-secrets-sync`, `update-files`, `restart`, `shutdown`, `rebuild`, ops escapes (`ws-placement-ops`, `app-version-ops`, smokes), `stack-rm`.

Retired Make names (never revive): `make sync` → swarm-sync; `make refresh`; `make stack-env-refresh` / public `make stack-deploy`.

Legacy: **`scripts/bootstrap/mongo-setup.sh`** — not Swarm CMD; not SoT. Live mongo ensure is `dataplane.EnsureMongo`.
